function creditBody(locale){ const b={fr:[frSafe,'Crédit immobilier Maroc en septembre 2026 : taux, mensualités et coût réel','Les mensualités ci-dessous sont des simulations à 4,8 % hors assurance et frais. Elles ne sont pas des offres bancaires.','cadre S.A.F.E d’analyse immobilière'],en:[enSafe,'Morocco mortgage rates in September 2026: rates, payments and real cost','The payments below are simulations at 4.8% excluding insurance and fees. They are not bank offers.','S.A.F.E property-analysis framework'],es:[esSafe,'Crédito hipotecario en Marruecos en septiembre de 2026: tasas, cuotas y coste real','Las cuotas son simulaciones al 4,8% sin seguro ni gastos. No son ofertas bancarias.','marco S.A.F.E de análisis inmobiliario'],nl:[nlSafe,'Hypotheek in Marokko in september 2026: rente, maandlasten en echte kost','De maandlasten zijn simulaties tegen 4,8% zonder verzekering en kosten. Het zijn geen bankaanbiedingen.','S.A.F.E-kader voor vastgoedanalyse']}[locale]; return `${commonBody(locale).l.date}\n\n${img('credit-immobilier-maroc-septembre-2026', locale==='fr'?'Bank Al-Maghrib à Rabat, repère institutionnel pour les taux et conditions de crédit au Maroc.':locale==='en'?'Bank Al-Maghrib in Rabat, institutional reference for Moroccan lending conditions.':locale==='es'?'Bank Al-Maghrib en Rabat, referencia institucional para las condiciones de crédito.':'Bank Al-Maghrib in Rabat, institutionele referentie voor kredietvoorwaarden.', b[2])}\n\n## ${b[1]}\n\nBank Al-Maghrib is the official reference for lending-rate surveys, while brokers and banks show the dispersion by borrower profile. In mid-2026, public market reporting pointed to mortgage rates around 4% for the strongest profiles, with broad ranges closer to 4.5%–5.5% depending on bank, duration, income stability, down payment and insurance.\n\n${mortgageTable(locale)}\n\n## Fixed or variable, and what changes the real cost\n\nThe headline rate is not the full cost. A buyer must add insurance, file fees, notary and registration costs, valuation, possible mortgage fees and the opportunity cost of the down payment. Longer duration lowers the monthly payment but increases total interest. A borrower can qualify for credit while the underlying property remains a weak investment. That is why the ${b[0](b[3])} separates financing capacity from property quality.\n\n## Source distinction\n\nOfficial data: Bank Al-Maghrib rate surveys and monetary-policy context. Market data: broker and bank indications. Simulations: editorial calculations, not binding offers.\n${faq(genericFaqs[locale])}`; }
