function rentBody(locale){ const b={fr:[frSafe,'Loyer à Marrakech en 2026 : prix des appartements quartier par quartier','analyse S.A.F.E d’un investissement immobilier'],en:[enSafe,'Marrakech rents in 2026: apartment prices by district','S.A.F.E analysis of a property investment'],es:[esSafe,'Alquiler en Marrakech en 2026: precios de apartamentos por barrio','análisis S.A.F.E de una inversión inmobiliaria'],nl:[nlSafe,'Huur in Marrakech in 2026: appartementprijzen per wijk','S.A.F.E-analyse van een vastgoedinvestering']}[locale]; return `${commonBody(locale).l.date}\n\n${img('loyer-marrakech-2026', locale==='fr'?'Hivernage à Marrakech, quartier résidentiel haut de gamme où les loyers varient selon les prestations.':locale==='en'?'Hivernage in Marrakech, a high-end residential district where rents vary by amenities.':locale==='es'?'Hivernage en Marrakech, barrio residencial de gama alta con alquileres variables.':'Hivernage in Marrakech, hoogwaardige woonwijk met uiteenlopende huren.', '')}\n\n## ${b[1]}\n\nRents in Marrakech are listing-driven and negotiation-sensitive. Signed leases may differ from advertised rents, especially when furniture, terrace, parking, pool, season and lease length are involved.\n\n${mdTable(['District','Studio / 1-bed','2-bed','3-bed','Comment'],[['Guéliz','3,500–5,500 DH','5,000–8,500 DH','7,000–12,000 DH','Central, liquid, expatriate demand.'],['Hivernage','4,500–7,000 DH','7,000–11,000 DH','10,000–16,000 DH','Premium buildings and furnished stock.'],['Agdal','4,000–6,500 DH','6,000–10,000 DH','8,000–14,000 DH','Modern family and student demand.'],['Targa','2,500–4,000 DH','3,500–6,000 DH','4,500–8,000 DH','Family areas, more car-dependent.'],['Palmeraie','4,000–7,000 DH','6,500–10,000 DH','9,000–18,000 DH','Large variance: apartments vs villas.'],['Route de l’Ourika','3,000–5,000 DH','5,000–8,000 DH','8,000–15,000 DH','Villas and nature-oriented demand.']])}\n\n## Furnished, unfurnished and seasonal effects\n\nA furnished apartment can command a premium, but it brings replacement, maintenance and inventory risk. Long-term rent is usually more predictable than short-term rent, yet the net result depends on vacancy, agency fees, deposit, charges, repairs and tax treatment. High advertised rent alone does not guarantee high yield; use an ${b[0](b[2])} to connect rent, price, charges and risk.\n\n## Data distinction\n\nThese are listing and agency observations, not official lease registrations. They should be used as negotiation ranges and checked with current comparable offers.\n${faq(genericFaqs[locale])}`; }
