function mreBody(locale){ const b={fr:[frSafe,'Aide au logement Maroc 2026 pour les MRE : conditions, montants et démarches depuis l’étranger','méthode S.A.F.E d’analyse immobilière'],en:[enSafe,'Morocco housing aid 2026 for MRE: conditions, amounts and steps from abroad','S.A.F.E real-estate analysis method'],es:[esSafe,'Ayuda vivienda Marruecos 2026 para MRE: condiciones, importes y trámites desde el extranjero','método S.A.F.E de análisis inmobiliario'],nl:[nlSafe,'Huisvestingssteun Marokko 2026 voor MRE: voorwaarden, bedragen en stappen vanuit het buitenland','S.A.F.E-methode voor vastgoedanalyse']}[locale]; return `${commonBody(locale).l.date}\n\n${img('aide-logement-mre-maroc-2026', locale==='fr'?'Entrée de l’aéroport Marrakech-Ménara, illustration des démarches immobilières à distance par des MRE.':locale==='en'?'Entrance to Marrakech-Menara Airport, illustrating property steps handled from abroad by MRE buyers.':locale==='es'?'Entrada del aeropuerto Marrakech-Menara, contexto de compradores MRE a distancia.':'Ingang van luchthaven Marrakech-Menara, context voor MRE-kopers op afstand.', '')}\n\n## ${b[1]}\n\nYes, an MRE can benefit from Morocco’s housing aid if the buyer and the home meet the same programme conditions. Public 2026 figures mention MRE beneficiaries representing around a quarter of the programme in some government updates. Residence abroad does not create a higher amount; it mainly changes the practical difficulty of verification, signatures, banking and timing.\n\n${mdTable(['Question','Answer'],[['Amount','100,000 DH up to 300,000 DH TTC; 70,000 DH above 300,000 and up to 700,000 DH TTC.'],['Specific MRE bonus','No documented separate bonus in the general programme.'],['Main practical issue','Distance: power of attorney, notary coordination, bank transfers, document checks.'],['Financing','Office des Changes rules and bank policy must be checked before payment.']])}\n\n## Practical checklist\n\n- Verify eligibility on Daam Sakane before paying.\n- Confirm the property price, first-sale status and administrative documents.\n- Use a limited, precise power of attorney if someone signs locally.\n- Keep bank transfer and foreign-exchange evidence.\n- Ask the notary to explain the State mortgage and possible release process.\n- Do not sign remotely on brochure or video alone.\n\nDistance makes project verification harder. A structured project-analysis process is therefore useful before signing remotely; the ${b[0](b[2])} can organize questions on price, documents, developer, legal clarity and delivery risk. It does not replace the Moroccan notary.\n\n## Source distinction\n\nProgramme amounts come from housing-aid sources. MRE financing and transfers must be checked against Office des Changes rules and the bank’s file requirements.\n${faq(genericFaqs[locale])}`; }
